<task id="025" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Implement admin-initiated CIAM provisioner (replace B2B invitation)</title>
    <phase>2 Identity + provisioning + document content</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <status-note>2026-07-19 COMPLETE. Replaced the Graph B2B invitation in InviteExternalUserEndpoint with idempotent CIAM account creation. New CiamUserProvisioningService (concrete singleton, ADR-010/§11-justified): CreateCiamUserAsync generates a temp password (PasswordGenerator), builds the CIAM local-account payload via pure/static BuildCiamUser (email identities block, issuer=Ciam:Domain, ForceChangePasswordNextSignIn=true, PasswordPolicies=DisablePasswordExpiration — the testable seam for 030 crit.4), and POSTs via task-022 CiamGraphClientFactory.CreateClientForAppAsync (app-only, no OBO, no B2B guest). Endpoint flow: resolve-or-create Contact (existing DataverseWebApiClient logic, extended to read sprk_externalobjectid) → IDEMPOTENCY GATE (existingOid populated ⇒ return AlreadyProvisioned, NO 2nd account) → CreateCiamUserAsync → UpdateAsync persist oid → SendCiamOnboardingEmailAsync (task 024, portalUrl from ExternalAccess:PortalUrl config, un-encoded=trusted). Removed SendB2BInvitationAsync/Invitation/IGraphClientFactory/Microsoft.Graph.Models usings. Temp password never returned/logged. Response DTO shape kept (InviteRedeemUrl→portalUrl, Status=Provisioned|AlreadyProvisioned). Registered in ExternalAccessModule. Config added: Ciam:Domain + ExternalAccess:PortalUrl (placeholders). NOTE: POML said reuse RegistrationDataverseService resolve-or-create, but that service handles sprk_registrationrequest (not contacts) — used the endpoint's existing DataverseWebApiClient contact logic instead (directional-mode deviation). Build 0 errors (ObjectIdentity/PasswordPolicies compile on Graph SDK 5.101.0); publish 45.69 MB (≤60, no new package). code-review+adr-check clean. Hardening edge filed: DI-025-01 (create-ok/persist-fail window — safe today, no dup account). Tests: task 030.</status-note>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth-sensitive multi-file provisioning replacing the B2B flow (tags: auth)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth-sensitive multi-file provisioning replacing B2B flow</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>Complex multi-file change with a complete spec (account creation + oid persist + email + idempotency)</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-safe-reason>modifies InviteExternalUserEndpoint + wires client/email/schema</parallel-safe-reason>
    <deps>022, 004, 024</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1.5-2 dev-days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Replace the Graph B2B invitation in `InviteExternalUserEndpoint` with CIAM account creation via the cross-tenant CIAM Graph client (task 022): Graph `POST /users` with an email local-account `identities` block, temp password + `forceChangePasswordNextSignIn`, `passwordPolicies: DisablePasswordExpiration`; persist the returned `oid` to `Contact.sprk_externalobjectid`; send the onboarding email (task 024). The flow MUST be idempotent — skip account creation when an oid is already present. Reuse `GraphUserService` payload shape, `PasswordGenerator`, `TrackingIdGenerator`, and `RegistrationDataverseService` resolve-or-create-by-email. Do NOT create a workforce B2B guest.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    You are a BFF identity engineer replacing the external B2B invitation flow with an idempotent admin-initiated CIAM provisioner, reusing the existing registration building blocks.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `InviteExternalUserEndpoint` resolves-or-creates a Dataverse `Contact` by email, and — if no `oid` is bound — creates a CIAM account via the cross-tenant Graph client (`POST /users` with email `identities` local account, temp password + `forceChangePasswordNextSignIn`, `passwordPolicies: DisablePasswordExpiration`), persists the returned `oid` to `Contact.sprk_externalobjectid`, and sends the onboarding email; re-invoking for a Contact that already has an oid creates NO second account (idempotent). No workforce B2B guest is created.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per ADR-028 Amendment A1, the external portal moves off Entra B2B guests to CIAM broker-only. `InviteExternalUserEndpoint` currently issues a Graph B2B invitation; this task replaces that step with CIAM account creation via the task-022 cross-tenant client. The reusable building blocks (from the BFF audit): `GraphUserService.CreateUserAsync` payload shape + `PasswordGenerator` (temp password), `TrackingIdGenerator`, and `RegistrationDataverseService` resolve-or-create-by-email + idempotency guard. The CIAM-specific additions are the `identities` (email local account) block on the user payload and persisting the returned `oid` to `Contact.sprk_externalobjectid` (task 004 column). Onboarding email is task 024. Steps are prescriptive because the sequence (create → persist oid → email, guarded by idempotency) is auth-critical.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs</file>
      <file status="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/GraphUserService.cs</file>
      <file status="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/PasswordGenerator.cs</file>
      <file status="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/TrackingIdGenerator.cs</file>
      <file status="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: the invite endpoint. MUST create a CIAM account (broker-only) and MUST NOT provision a workforce Entra B2B guest; the external user's token is never exchanged downstream (Amendment A1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-FR-08">Scope: idempotency. MUST be idempotent — when the resolved Contact already has an `oid` (`sprk_externalobjectid`), SKIP account creation (no second CIAM account); reuse `RegistrationDataverseService` resolve-or-create-by-email + the idempotency guard.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-FR-08">Scope: the user payload. Reuse the `GraphUserService.CreateUserAsync` payload shape + `PasswordGenerator`; add the CIAM `identities` (email local account) block, temp password + `forceChangePasswordNextSignIn`, `passwordPolicies: DisablePasswordExpiration`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-FR-08">Scope: oid persistence. MUST persist the Graph-returned `oid` to `Contact.sprk_externalobjectid` and send the onboarding email (task 024 method) after successful creation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">Scope: the CIAM credential. Use the task-022 client (KV cert / MI-as-FIC) — no plaintext secret; the temp password is generated by `PasswordGenerator`, not hardcoded.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this BFF task. State the §10 BFF Hygiene Placement Justification in the PR description (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`), and report BFF compressed publish size + diff vs baseline (~49.63 MB) confirming the ≤60 MB ceiling (NFR-01). Add/update tests per §10 bullet 6 (covered by task 030).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <justification>
    <existing>`InviteExternalUserEndpoint` performs a Graph B2B invitation.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — replace the B2B step in the existing endpoint with CIAM account creation; reuse GraphUserService payload/PasswordGenerator/TrackingIdGenerator/RegistrationDataverseService.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the CIAM provisioner, no CIAM identity is minted for outside counsel — admin-initiated onboarding is impossible and the primary R1 use case fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/GraphUserService.cs</file>
      <file>.claude/agent-memory/researcher/ciam-user-provisioning-graph-2026-07-19.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>Read `InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs`, `GraphUserService.cs` (payload shape), `PasswordGenerator.cs`, `TrackingIdGenerator.cs`, and `RegistrationDataverseService.cs` to identify the B2B step to replace and the reusable helpers.</step>
    <step>Resolve-or-create the Dataverse `Contact` by email via `RegistrationDataverseService`; read its `sprk_externalobjectid`.</step>
    <step>Idempotency gate: if `sprk_externalobjectid` is already populated, SKIP account creation (do not call Graph `POST /users`); proceed to grant/email as appropriate without minting a second account.</step>
    <step>If no oid is bound, build the Graph `POST /users` payload reusing the `GraphUserService` shape + `PasswordGenerator` temp password, adding the CIAM email `identities` local-account block, `forceChangePasswordNextSignIn=true`, and `passwordPolicies: DisablePasswordExpiration`; create the user via the task-022 cross-tenant CIAM Graph client.</step>
    <step>Persist the Graph-returned `oid` to `Contact.sprk_externalobjectid`.</step>
    <step>Send the onboarding email via `RegistrationEmailService.SendCiamOnboardingEmailAsync` (task 024).</step>
    <step>Ensure no Graph B2B invitation path remains reachable for the external flow.</step>
    <step>Build and run `dotnet publish -c Release`; record compressed size + diff vs the ~49.63 MB baseline.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Graph `POST /users` contract (the `identities` block or `passwordProfile`/`passwordPolicies` shape) differs from the researcher spike spec (`ciam-user-provisioning-graph-2026-07-19.md`), STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 rather than adapting the payload by guesswork.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output>`InviteExternalUserEndpoint` creating a CIAM account (idempotent), persisting oid, and sending the onboarding email.</output>
    <output>B2B invitation path removed from the external flow.</output>
    <output>BFF publish-size report (compressed size + diff).</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Inviting a new Contact creates a CIAM account, persists the returned `oid` to `sprk_externalobjectid`, and sends the onboarding email.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (idempotency): re-invoking for a Contact whose `sprk_externalobjectid` is already populated creates NO second CIAM account.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no workforce Entra B2B guest is created for the external user.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The created user carries the email `identities` local account, `forceChangePasswordNextSignIn`, and `passwordPolicies: DisablePasswordExpiration`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF compressed publish size is reported with diff and stays ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on task 022 (cross-tenant CIAM Graph client), task 004 (`sprk_externalobjectid` column), and task 024 (onboarding email method). Prescriptive steps because the create→persist→email sequence guarded by idempotency is auth-critical.
  </notes>

